# CubeCom = The Digital Product Stage

Full constitution: `docs/design-system.md` · living: `apps/docs/design-principles`

## Signature (four things only)

1. Mineral-white digital stage (perspective horizon + soft light — not a flat card)
2. Physical product as hero on that stage
3. Violet spatial plane / light (transformation — same logic on stage, nav glow, surfaces)
4. Very large, tight black typography

Hero, sidebar active state, and content surfaces must speak the same spatial language.

## Do this

- Product surfaces use `.cube-stage` with perspective horizon, dimensional violet plane, product hero, grounded shadow
- Repeat the same spatial violet lightly on: sidebar active (edge + glow), `.cube-surface` cards (corner light)
- UI chrome: white / black / neutral gray, excellent type, generous whitespace
- Wordmark: simple `cubecom` (+ `Pro` as tier) — fixed lockup, not UI type
- Type locked: Hero 56/0.96/700 · Page 32/1.05/650 · H2 21/600 · Card 16/600 · Body 14/1.55/#555
- Tight display only for major statements; stop iterating fonts — refine surfaces/spacing
- Cards: quiet borders, more padding, subtler directional light, natural height

## Never do this

- Technical grids, square nodes, diagonal cuts, sci-fi metadata
- Dark cyber sidebars, violet nav rails/pills as brand
- Flooding UI with purple or decorating every control

## Ecosystem

Backoffice thumbs / 3D / Customizer / Logo editor / docs covers / marketing = Stage.  
Tables, forms, filters = neutral working UI.
